ing the width of the stone",{"_":51,"ana":52,"ref":53},{"lettering":455,"dimensions":456},"Plain wide letters: kappa has arms of almost full length, not quite joining the vertical; rho is closed; alpha broad with straight bar; sigma has horizontal top and bottom bars, joined by a curving stroke rather than two distinct diagonals; omega sits very slightly above the line, is circular and open with short arms",[457,458],{"type":58,"l":59,"from":60,"to":60,"h":63,"unit":62,"atLeast":63,"atMost":63},{"type":66,"l":67,"from":60,"to":68,"h":69,"unit":62},{"_":460,"notBefore":461,"notAfter":462,"evidence":463},"Dated to the end of the 4th century BCE by the burial goods",-325,-301,"archaeological-context",[465,466],{"_":76,"type":77,"ref":78,"region":79},{"_":81,"type":82,"ref":83,"offset":84,"region":79},[468],[87,88],[90,91],{"_":471,"role":96,"ref":472},"Museo Archeologico Santi Furnari di Tripi","http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/museum/177",{"_":474,"type":100},"ME23435",{"_":102,"mainLang":103,"languages":476},[102],[478],{"atLeast":107,"atMost":107},[420,480,114,481],"Bacci, Coppolino, Sofia, Arizia, 2015, Tripi. Il museo archeologico \"Santi Furnari\". Guida all'esposizione","Sofia, 2018, Nuove iscrizioni funerarie dalla necropoli di Abakainon",[424,483,120,484],"ILQ4RQGU","JQQKI6JP",[486,487,488,32,36,40,125,126,127,128,126,489,131,103],"isic004411","epitaph for kratisstos",{"_":209},"museo archeologico santi furnari di tripi","\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>Κρατίσστω \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>",{"author":3,"date":4,"citedRange":492,"ptr":493,"ref":494,"inscriptionDate":4,"title":2,"citation":5,"uri":6,"year":4},"113 fig.115",{"target":136},{"_":138,"target":138},{"file":496,"uri":496,"title":497,"status":498,"editions":499,"editionAuthor":30,"type":505,"objectType":506,"material":510,"condition":46,"layoutDesc":512,"handNote":516,"date":521,"places":525,"geo":529,"country":79,"provenance":76,"provenanceGeo":531,"region":92,"settlement":81,"repository":532,"idno":536,"textLang":537,"tmNumber":46,"letterHeights":539,"publications":541,"zotero":542,"keywords":543,"html":548,"bibl":549,"bulletinDateSort":139,"citedRangeSort":492,"languageSort":102,"materialSort":40,"typeSort":32},"ISic004417","Epitaph for [-?-], child of Gerontios",{"_":209},[500,501,502,503,504],{"type":16},{"type":19},{"type":21},{"type":24},{"type":27},{"_":32,"ana":33,"ref":34},{"_":507,"ana":508,"ref":509},"plinth","#object.arch_element.plinth","https://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/1910.html",{"_":40,"ana":41,"type":42,"subtype":511,"ref":45},[44],{"layout":513},{"p":514,"rs":515,"damage":46},"Remains of two lines of Greek letters, apparently centred on the face of the plinth; the second line sits directly above the lower moulding",{"_":51,"ana":52,"ref":53},{"lettering":517,"dimensions":518},"Simple, widely spaced letters. Omega is wide and open, with horizontal tails; rho has a large, closed eye; omicron is small and mid-line; nu is regular and with both verticals full length",[519,520],{"type":58,"l":168,"from":60,"to":68,"h":63,"unit":62,"atLeast":63,"atMost":63},{"type":66,"l":67,"from":60,"to":68,"unit":62},{"_":522,"notBefore":523,"notAfter":524,"evidence":463},"The tomb has not been excavated fully, but the cemetery went out of use around the end of the 3rd century BCE or early 2nd century, offering a terminus ante quem",-350,-201,[526,528],{"_":76,"type":77,"ref":78,"corresp":527,"region":79},"#findspot",{"_":81,"type":82,"ref":83,"offset":84,"region":79},[530],[87,88],[90,91],{"_":533,"role":534,"ref":535},"Necropoli di Abakainon","site","http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/museum/186",{"type":100},{"_":102,"mainLang":103,"languages":538},[102],[540],{"atLeast":107,"atMost":107},[420,114,481],[424,120,484],[544,545,546,32,507,40,125,126,127,128,126,547,131